  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 940 PM CST WED NOV 25 2026\n\nWe were treated to a rather dreary day across Central Alabama\ntoday. However, we did receive some much needed rainfall. Radar\nrainfall estimates as of 7 PM this evening show roughly 0.5-1.5\"\nacross the region. Light to moderate rainfall will continue for\nseveral more hours with clearing likely as a cold front passes\nthrough. With that said, we will see a few batches of light rain\nthrough the day Thursday as moisture wraps around the upper level\nlow. There is a low chance for some very light snow across our\nfar northern counties as much cooler air arrives as the last of\nthe moisture is exiting the region. Forecast guidance continues\nto struggle with temps tonight so we went ahead and followed the\nsame tempo as previous shifts and nudged lows tonight up a tad.\n\nA cold front clearing the area will leave dry and chilly\nconditions for Thanksgiving. Breezy northwesterly winds will hold\nhigh temperatures in the mid-40s to low 50s on Thursday, with\ntemperatures potentially peaking early in the day before dropping\nthrough the afternoon. Overnight lows will fall into the mid-20s\nto low 30s Friday and Saturday morning. Southerly flow quickly\nresumes on Saturday, warming temperatures several degrees.\nAnother upper trough heads our way over the weekend, eventually\nsending a cold front through the region late Sunday into Monday.\nMoisture recovery looks to be sufficient enough to warrant a\n50-80% chance of rain as this system moves through. Instability \nwill be lacking so not expecting any strong to severe storms at \nthis time.\n\n95/Castillo",
